# Build output of `grim-indexer build`.
dist/

# NOT ignored: `public/` is this index's own asset layer - the logo and
# favicon `index.config.json` names live there, and the build copies it into
# `dist/`. Ignoring it means the site references files the deploy never had.

# Renderer scratch dir - removed on a clean build, left behind by a killed one.
.index-*/

node_modules/
.npm/

# NOT ignored: `package-lock.json` is what pins the renderer this index builds
# and validates with. Committing it is what makes `npm ci` in CI reproducible.

# Per-session agent telemetry written by the model-routing hook, not config.
.claude/state/

# Skills `grim install` vendors in from `grimoire.toml`. They are dependencies,
# not sources: `grimoire.lock` pins each to a digest, so committing the
# unpacked copies is the node_modules mistake. `research-lang` beside them IS
# tracked - it is authored here and appears in no lockfile.
.claude/skills/ai-config-authoring/
.claude/skills/grim-authoring/
.claude/skills/grim-usage/

# Python bytecode and tooling caches. `.claude/skills/research-lang/scripts/`
# and `tests/` are tracked, so a stray `__pycache__` would be committed next
# to them. `grim build` already excludes them from a published layer (the
# digest is identical with and without), but nothing should get that far.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/

.DS_Store
